[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
I was touched when you accepted a request from me, a stranger, so easily. You must truly be one of those good, heroic adventurers. Are you interested in setting out on an ocean voyage?|pt|Fiquei emocionado quando você aceitou um pedido meu, um estranho, com tanta facilidade. 
[|pt|[[
I've sailed a few times... But now that I think about it, I've never gone across the continent.|pt|Já naveguei algumas vezes... Mas pensando bem, nunca atravessei o continente.
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
No, that's good enough. I may just have one small fishing vessel, but I used to be a captain that commanded a fleet.|pt|Não, isso é bom o suficiente. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
As you may know after a few sea voyages, not many people have gone across the ocean beyond the continent. I too have failed to conquer the ocean.|pt|Como você deve saber, depois de algumas viagens marítimas, poucas pessoas cruzaram o oceano além do continente. 
^0000ffMr. Janssen talked about his perilous ocean journeys for quite a while. You have enough time on your hands, so you sit down, quietly listening to his story.^000000|pt|^0000ffMr. 
^0000ffAt least half of his story sounded grossly exaggerated, but something caught your ear: he insists that a humongous tower exists on the ocean, and that it's so tall, it scrapes across the sky.^000000|pt|_Pelo menos metade de sua história parecia extremamente exagerada, mas algo chamou sua atenção: ele insiste que existe uma torre enorme no oceano e que é tão alta que arranha o céu.^000000
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
So all I could do was cast anchor at that humongous tower after my fleet was wrecked. At first, we were only going to stay there until the rainstorm was over, but it didn't end as soon as we had hoped.|pt|Então tudo que pude fazer foi lançar âncora naquela torre enorme depois que minha frota naufragou. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
My crew was starving, and a few of them walked into the tower in order to find food... They never came back.|pt|Minha tripulação estava morrendo de fome e alguns deles entraram na torre em busca de comida... Eles nunca mais voltaram.
[|pt|[[
Why didn't you go in there with them?|pt|Por que você não foi lá com eles?
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
My instincts told me that tower was dangerous. I was curious, but I wasn't going to risk my life. We waited for them to come back for 7 days until the rainstorm was finally over, but no one returned.|pt|Meus instintos me disseram que aquela torre era perigosa. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
In our desperation to survive, we abandoned all our goods, and left the tower only with a little bit of the water and edible plants we'd found around the tower. When we finally reached land, I was the only one alive...|pt|Em nosso desespero para sobreviver, abandonamos todos os nossos bens e saímos da torre apenas com um pouco da água e das plantas comestíveis que encontramos ao redor da torre. 
^0000ffYou could imagine the heartwretching scene of the dying fleet on their last voyage, even if he didn't explain it any further. A look of somber regret swept over his face as he remained silent a while, and then he said:^000000|pt|^0000ffY você poderia imaginar a cena desoladora da frota moribunda em sua última viagem, mesmo que ele não explicasse mais nada. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
I have something I must do before I die. I must retrieve the remains of my crew that died in the tower, and give them a proper burial.|pt|Tenho algo que devo fazer antes de morrer. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
I feel so lucky to meet a warm-hearted adventurer like you. With the money you've given me, I can finally go sailing to the tower again.|pt|Sinto-me muito sortudo por conhecer um aventureiro de coração caloroso como você. 
[|pt|[[
How about hiring me as your first mate?|pt|Que tal me contratar como seu primeiro imediato?
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
Thank you, but it is an extremely dangerous place. I have my duty to fulfill, but you don't have any obligation to me or them. I don't wish to sacrifice someone as young as you to such a dangerous place.|pt|Obrigado, mas é um lugar extremamente perigoso. 
[|pt|[[
No...|pt|Não...
.|pt|.
.|pt|.
As an adventurer, there's my obligation to those in need. I'm also very curious about that place...|pt|Como aventureiro, essa é minha obrigação para com os necessitados. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
I was going to leave right away, but since you've joined me, I should give you time to prepare. I'll be waiting here until you're ready to go.|pt|Eu ia partir imediatamente, mas como você se juntou a mim, deveria lhe dar tempo para se preparar. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
...Okay then...|pt|...Tudo bem então...
Welcome aboard, first mate.|pt|Bem-vindo a bordo, primeiro imediato.
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
Shall we leave now?|pt|Vamos embora agora?
Yes, let's go!:No, I'm not quite ready...|pt|Sim, vamos!:Não, ainda não estou pronto...
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
Then pull up the anchor, first mate!|pt|Então levante a âncora, primeiro imediato!
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
Sure, no problem. Come back when you're ready.|pt|Claro, não há problema. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
Well, to travel the ocean again, we need to restock on goods. If you give me 10,000 Zeny, I'll take care of the rest.|pt|Bem, para viajar pelo oceano novamente, precisamos reabastecer as mercadorias. 
I'll come back later.:Let's go, now!|pt|Vou voltar mais tarde.:Vamos, agora!
[|pt|[[
I'm sorry, but I don't have that much money. I'll come back when I save enough.|pt|Sinto muito, mas não tenho tanto dinheiro. 
[Captain Janssen]|pt|[Captain Janssen]
