This place has so many people coming in and out of it, it's hard to keep track of every one of them.|pt|Este lugar tem tantas pessoas entrando e saindo que é difícil acompanhar cada uma delas.
[Carola Firth]|pt|[Carola Firth]
Some workers went down to the basement for repair work and heard strange rustling noises.|pt|Alguns trabalhadores desceram ao porão para fazer reparos e ouviram barulhos estranhos.
When they found the source of noise? kyaaaahhh!|pt|Quando encontraram a fonte do ruído? 
[Carola Firth]|pt|[Carola Firth]
Lucas! Do you want me to kill you? Stop doing that!|pt|Lucas! 
Aww, I'm too scared to talk about this anymore.|pt|Ah, estou com muito medo de falar mais sobre isso.
[Lucas Richie]|pt|[Lucas Richie]
The basement is haunted. You don't really believe that, do you?|pt|O porão está assombrado. 
I think there are treasures down there.|pt|Acho que há tesouros lá embaixo.
[Lucas Richie]|pt|[Lucas Richie]
And whoever spread that stupid rumor, he did it to keep others from finding out about the treasures.|pt|E quem espalhou esse boato estúpido fez isso para impedir que outros descobrissem os tesouros.
[Lucas Richie]|pt|[Lucas Richie]
Hm, I meant that as a joke, but maybe she really is scared.|pt|Hm, eu quis dizer isso como uma piada, mas talvez ela esteja realmente assustada.
What do you say, Carola? How'd you like to go down there with me?|pt|O que você me diz, Carola? 
Ah, adventurer. Let's keep this just between you and me, okay?|pt|Ah, aventureiro. 
Woof, woof! Woof, woof!|pt|Uau, uau! 
[Bounty Hunter]|pt|[Bounty Hunter]
What am I looking at? Ah, those buffaloes. There's a large sum of money offered for their heads.|pt|O que estou olhando? 
[Bounty Hunter]|pt|[Bounty Hunter]
The Vigilantes and the Sheriff have had enough with them, now that they started robbing the train.|pt|Os Vigilantes e o Xerife estão fartos deles, agora que começaram a roubar o trem.
[Bounty Hunter]|pt|[Bounty Hunter]
But thanks to them, I've got a lucrative job.|pt|Mas graças a eles, tenho um emprego lucrativo.
[Shepherd]|pt|[Shepherd]
I'm sorry, guys. I should've never taken you here...|pt|Sinto muito, pessoal. 
[Shepherd]|pt|[Shepherd]
I didn't know there was no grass here.|pt|Eu não sabia que não havia grama aqui.
[Shepherd]|pt|[Shepherd]
Just hang in there. I'm growing some grass for you out there. If it grows well, you wouldn't have to be hungry anymore.|pt|Apenas aguente firme. 
[Joyce Leslie]|pt|[Joyce Leslie]
The houses closer to the beach have always been prone to sinking, long before the first level was buried.|pt|As casas mais próximas da praia sempre estiveram sujeitas a afundar, muito antes de o primeiro nível ter sido soterrado.
This house sank little by little, until the ground couldn't hold its weight anymore.|pt|Esta casa foi afundando aos poucos, até que o chão não aguentou mais o seu peso.
[Joyce Leslie]|pt|[Joyce Leslie]
What happened to its residents, you ask? You're an adventurer, why do you care?|pt|O que aconteceu com seus residentes, você pergunta? 
[Joyce Leslie]|pt|[Joyce Leslie]
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to get angry with you.|pt|Me desculpe, eu não queria ficar com raiva de você.
It's just that... things haven't been good.|pt|É que... as coisas não têm estado bem.
[Joyce Leslie]|pt|[Joyce Leslie]
But at least I have work to do and food to eat, thanks to some people.|pt|Mas pelo menos tenho trabalho para fazer e comida para comer, graças a algumas pessoas.
Where do I get work and food? Head up to the eastern gate. You'll see the along the way.|pt|Onde consigo trabalho e comida? 
[Joe]|pt|[Joe]
...|pt|...
[Joe]|pt|[Joe]
You're too weak|pt|Você é muito fraco
to enter the basement.|pt|para entrar no porão.
Please leave.|pt|Por favor, saia.
[Joe]|pt|[Joe]
...|pt|...
[Joe]|pt|[Joe]
Are you going to go in?|pt|Você vai entrar?
[Donovan]|pt|[Donovan]
...|pt|...
[Joe]|pt|[Joe]
You'd better get out of there|pt|É melhor você sair daí
as soon as you're done.|pt|assim que terminar.
Hungry Laborer: Aww, I'm starving. Why isn't the line getting any shorter?|pt|Trabalhador Faminto: Ah, estou morrendo de fome. 
Curious Person: What's this line for? Are you waiting to get event prizes?|pt|Pessoa curiosa: Para que serve esta linha? 
Hungry Laborer: This is ridiculous. I've been waiting in line for 3 hours to eat.|pt|Trabalhador Faminto: Isso é ridículo. 
Hungry Laborer: Soon it'll be my turn!|pt|Trabalhador Faminto: Em breve será a minha vez!
Hungry Laborer: Hey, don't you see the line here? Get to the end of the line!|pt|Trabalhador Faminto: Ei, você não vê a fila aqui? 
[Smell Maniac]|pt|[Smell Maniac]
*Sniff Sniff* Doesn't this place smell good to you? I love its salty, dank, musty smell! I could live here for the rest of my life!|pt|*Sniff Sniff* Este lugar não cheira bem para você? 
[Smell Maniac]|pt|[Smell Maniac]
...If only there weren't so many bugs. I'm just going to bottle the smell and take it with me.|pt|...Se ao menos não houvesse tantos bugs. 
[Unemployed Man]|pt|[Unemployed Man]
See those sea anemones? They keep clogging up the sewer pipes, so we get rid of them on a regular basis. I like sitting here and watching them move. And when I do, time goes by so quickly.|pt|Vê aquelas anêmonas do mar? 
[Unemployed Man]|pt|[Unemployed Man]
At least during that time I could forget my reality, about the mine, not having jobs, you know, that sort of thing.|pt|Pelo menos naquela época eu conseguia esquecer da minha realidade, da mina, de não ter emprego, sabe, esse tipo de coisa.
[Unemployed Man]|pt|[Unemployed Man]
I'm here because I have nowhere else to go, but I'll go back up once those who took up residence in the mine are gone.|pt|Estou aqui porque não tenho para onde ir, mas voltarei a subir assim que aqueles que fixaram residência na mina tiverem ido embora.
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
This place hasn't changed at all.|pt|Este lugar não mudou nada.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Remember when we first came here?|pt|Lembra quando viemos aqui pela primeira vez?
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
I do.|pt|Eu faço.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
We built this house from scratch, on our own from the foundation stones to the roofing.|pt|Construímos esta casa do zero, por conta própria, desde a pedra fundamental até a cobertura.
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
Aww, it's getting chilly. Let's go back up.|pt|Ah, está ficando frio. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
My lovely Clementine... I proposed to her here.|pt|Minha adorável Clementine... eu a pedi em casamento aqui.
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
I'm here.|pt|Estou aqui.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
My Clementine is not so old!|pt|Minha Clementine não é tão velha!
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
Grr, you senile coot!|pt|Grr, seu idiota senil!
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Mm? Who's there? Is it you, Charlie?|pt|Hum? 
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
Charlie can't come here. He lives across the sea.|pt|Charlie não pode vir aqui. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Does he? By the way, this place has changed a lot.|pt|Ele faz? 
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
No, it hasn't. It's just the same as when we left it.|pt|Não, não foi. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Is it? I come here when I miss the old days, but it's too dark. By the way, why has it become so wet?|pt|É isso? 
[Old Woman]|pt|[Old Woman]
It was flooded. That's why it had to be filled up and we had to move up. Have you gone senile? You were the one who insisted this place was too low to build houses on.|pt|Foi inundado. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Was I?|pt|Eu estava?
[Kid]|pt|[Kid]
Mommy, when can we live above ground again?|pt|Mamãe, quando poderemos viver na superfície novamente?
[Mom]|pt|[Mom]
Soon. When Daddy can go work at the mine again. When Mommy and Daddy make enough money to buy back the house.|pt|Breve. 
[Kid]|pt|[Kid]
I want to go home...|pt|Eu quero ir para casa...
[Mom]|pt|[Mom]
I haven't been able to feed my child well. I can't remember the last time he had a decent meal.|pt|Não tenho conseguido alimentar bem meu filho. 
[Kid]|pt|[Kid]
Mommy, I'm okay.|pt|Mamãe, estou bem.
[Mom]|pt|[Mom]
Let's wait for Daddy. He'll be back with food.|pt|Vamos esperar pelo papai. 
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
What, haven't you seen a Buffalo Bandit before?|pt|O quê, você nunca viu um Buffalo Bandit antes?
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
Don't give me that dirty look. We're not doing anything bad right now, now are we?|pt|Não me olhe com esse olhar sujo. 
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
You're on our turf. Don't cause trouble, and stay away from here.|pt|Você está em nosso território. 
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
I'll let you come and go, if you promise me not to tell anyone above the ground about us. Promise?|pt|Vou deixar você ir e vir, se você me prometer não contar a ninguém sobre nós. 
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
Aside from the main gate, there are are a few more entrances that only we know, and we guard one of them.|pt|Além do portão principal, existem mais algumas entradas que só nós conhecemos, e guardamos uma delas.
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
Why are you telling me this?|pt|Por que você está me contando isso?
[Buffalo Bandit]|pt|[Buffalo Bandit]
So you'd be scared and want to stay away.|pt|Então você ficaria com medo e quereria ficar longe.
[Dispatched Nun]|pt|[Dispatched Nun]
Can you believe some people actually live here? People above ground don't care about them. Officially, this place is vacant, even though it's not.|pt|Você acredita que algumas pessoas realmente moram aqui? 
[Dispatched Nun]|pt|[Dispatched Nun]
They don't want to know or care. You have to be in a pretty bad situation to end up here.|pt|Eles não querem saber ou se importar. 
[Erekter]|pt|[Erekter]
Erekter wants to become the best netter in the village when he grows up.|pt|Erekter quer se tornar o melhor rededor da vila quando crescer.
[Erekter]|pt|[Erekter]
The best netter in the village is Mrs. Soft Feather.|pt|A melhor rede da vila é a Sra. Soft Feather.
[Erekter]|pt|[Erekter]
Mm... Then I'll become the second-best netter in the village!|pt|Mm... Então me tornarei o segundo melhor goleiro da vila!
[Soft Feather]|pt|[Soft Feather]
Ho ho ho, there's not a single fishing net in the village that hasn't been handled by me.|pt|Ho ho ho, não há uma única rede de pesca na aldeia que não tenha sido manejada por mim.
There are others who make good nets, but I'm the one who gives the nets their finishing touch.|pt|Há outros que fazem boas redes, mas sou eu quem dá o toque final às redes.
[Erekter]|pt|[Erekter]
I want to learn from you too! I want to become as good at netting as you!|pt|Quero aprender com você também! 
[Soft Feather]|pt|[Soft Feather]
Your hands are too soft right now. Go out and play. I'll teach you when your hands become tougher.|pt|Suas mãos estão muito moles agora. 
[Soft Feather]|pt|[Soft Feather]
Yes, I'll teach you how to net. For now, let me teach you how to make pretty knots with grass blades.|pt|Sim, vou te ensinar como fazer rede. 
