[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
You'll have to trust him. Ezekiel may not look like much in your eyes, but he's pretty good, right?|pt|Você terá que confiar nele. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
No, the time is...!|pt|Não, a hora é...!
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Ahhh... If only we had the right equipment... I could have done it faster... I can't help it.|pt|Ahhh... Se ao menos tivéssemos o equipamento certo... eu poderia ter feito isso mais rápido... não posso evitar.
[Joel]|pt|[Joel]
Aaaaaah!!! I'm dying!!!|pt|Aaaaaah!!! 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Adventurer, how's it going, can I start my construction?|pt|Aventureiro, como vai, posso começar minha construção?
About that...|pt|Sobre isso...
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I'm trying to keep it out of the way so it doesn't affect anything else, but I guess that doesn't work either.|pt|Estou tentando mantê-lo fora do caminho para que não afete mais nada, mas acho que também não funciona.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
But I can't give up, and I'm glad you're willing to come back and talk about it, but before then, I need to get a group of like-minded people together and get ready to convince them.|pt|Mas não posso desistir, e estou feliz que você esteja disposto a voltar e falar sobre isso, mas antes disso, preciso reunir um grupo de pessoas que pensam como você e me preparar para convencê-las.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I thought about doing what they said, but I can't. I don't know what else to do, but this is something I need to do.|pt|Pensei em fazer o que eles disseram, mas não consigo. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Speaking of which, Adventurer, I have a favor to ask.|pt|Falando nisso, Aventureiro, tenho um favor a pedir.
What is it?|pt|O que é?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
You can get most things here, but not Steel. Because of how difficult it is to bring it in, not to mention you need a lot of facilities to make Steel. So, Would it be okay if you bring me 3 of them? just 3...|pt|Você pode conseguir a maioria das coisas aqui, mas não Steel. 
I'll bring it to you.|pt|Eu vou trazer para você.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Thank you for your generosity. I'm glad you're so sympathetic to my cause and willing to help... I'll go get ready for construction.|pt|Obrigado pela sua generosidade. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Please convince <NAVI>[sir]<INFO>wolfvill,176,111,0,101,0</INFO></NAVI>that we need this facility.|pt|Por favor, convença <NAVI>[sir]<INFO>wolfvill,176,111,0,101,0</INFO></NAVI>de que precisamos desta instalação.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Ezekiel, you didn't come here to live a life of riches. You came here to do a job!|pt|Ezequiel, você não veio aqui para viver uma vida de riquezas. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
No, but to live here as myself is to really live. I am an eternal stranger here, am I not?|pt|Não, mas viver aqui como eu é viver de verdade. 
That person...?|pt|Essa pessoa...?
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Shhh- wait a minute, listen to what he's saying, he sounds like he's saying something.|pt|Shhh- espere um minuto, ouça o que ele está dizendo, parece que ele está dizendo alguma coisa.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
No, but I'm just as much an outsider here as I am there. Isn't that the same? Shouldn't I be more comfortable?|pt|Não, mas sou tão estranho aqui quanto lá. 
Maybe I should just give up and go home.|pt|Talvez eu devesse desistir e ir para casa.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
No, but that's what I initially aimed for. Finding my roots...|pt|Não, mas era isso que eu pretendia inicialmente. 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Ezekiel! How have you been? Why are you muttering to yourself like that?|pt|Ezequiel! 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Maram? Maram?? That's great. You know what, listen to me. You're busy? You're busy, but listen. Who am I going to tell this to? I don't even know anybody yet. So listen to me.|pt|Mara? 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I told you I was going to build a clinic here. When I came here, there was no decent clinic, so I build one.|pt|Eu disse que iria construir uma clínica aqui. 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
That's right. That's why I got a lot of things to fill it with this time.|pt|Isso mesmo. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I did that, but as soon as I started digging, the elders here stopped me. They say we should live in harmony with nature as we have done up until now, but they look at me as some sort of environmental destroyer. Am I that kind of person?|pt|Eu fiz isso, mas assim que comecei a cavar, os mais velhos daqui me pararam. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Is it really that destructive to nature and the environment to just build a more hygienic, more modern clinic, which would allow for a faster response in an emergency?|pt|É realmente tão destrutivo para a natureza e o meio ambiente apenas construir uma clínica mais higiênica e mais moderna, que permitiria uma resposta mais rápida em uma emergência?
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
No. You aren't that kind of person. Everyone else, but never you.|pt|Não. Você não é esse tipo de pessoa. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Isn't that right? And you've gotten me to the point where... I'm not doing anything right now because I'm thinking, Am I really a bad person?|pt|Não é verdade? 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
If that's the case, you should talk to Suad. That's not fair. We're all trying to live together. The clinic isn't against nature. Oh, come on.|pt|Se for esse o caso, você deveria falar com Suad. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Well... I talked to Suad... but he said there was nothing he could do and that he couldn't do what he wanted either.|pt|Bom... falei com Suad... mas ele disse que não podia fazer nada e que também não podia fazer o que queria.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I told him that we need a clinic, but we can't just push it through because the elderly people who have lived here for a long time are against it, so we have to convince them.|pt|Eu disse a ele que precisamos de uma clínica, mas não podemos simplesmente forçar porque os idosos que moram aqui há muito tempo são contra, então temos que convencê-los.
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
From the sounds of it, so does he. We can't ignore the opinions of the elders, after all, and it's not like Suad's the kind of guy who'd bend over backwards to do so.|pt|Pelo que parece, ele também. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
So... I'm... going back to Rachel... What do you think?|pt|Então... eu vou... voltar para Rachel... O que você acha?
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
What, you came this far and you're going back?|pt|O quê, você chegou até aqui e vai voltar?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
No, I didn't set out to go back... It's just that people are like that, they come here to have a better life, and if it's the same here or there, why wouldn't they want to stay where it's easier...|pt|Não, eu não pretendia voltar... É que as pessoas são assim, vêm aqui para ter uma vida melhor, e se é igual aqui ou ali, por que não querem ficar onde está? 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
So what I'm saying is... I'm trying to figure it out. When did I say I would just cut it and go back? Can you please not listen to me however you want?|pt|Então o que estou dizendo é... que estou tentando descobrir. 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Hmmm... but the clinic is a necessity as far as I'm concerned, and if I can make the case...|pt|Hmmm... mas a clínica é uma necessidade para mim, e se eu puder defender o caso...
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
That's right! I think the adventurer might be able to help us out. You know, this adventurer is really good at talking, don't you think his face makes him believable? This is just the kind of prize that grown-ups like.|pt|Isso mesmo! 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
He has a big heart, and he helped us buy and transport supplies.|pt|Ele tem um grande coração e nos ajudou a comprar e transportar suprimentos.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
He's a nice guy. He's a good man, yes, but...|pt|Ele é um cara legal. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
...Is that really the kind of person who gets the favor of the adults? They're so... so... stubborn.|pt|...Esse é realmente o tipo de pessoa que consegue o favor dos adultos? 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
You have to make the most of it. Even if I can't persuade you, what else is there to do but listen to more nagging? Is that the adventurer going to listen to that instead?|pt|Você tem que aproveitar ao máximo. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Well... Can I ask you a favor?|pt|Bem... Posso te pedir um favor?
Adventurer, do me a favor, we really need a modern clinic here, even if it's not as big as the one from Rachel.|pt|Aventureiro, me faça um favor, precisamos muito de uma clínica moderna aqui, mesmo que não seja tão grande quanto a da Rachel.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Where I am now, if I get hurt or sick, I have to rely on folk remedies from the past.|pt|Onde estou agora, se me machucar ou ficar doente, terei que confiar em remédios populares do passado.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I have some medicines and medical supplies from Rachel, but they are scarce, and I'm not in the right place to use them.|pt|Tenho alguns remédios e suprimentos médicos de Rachel, mas são escassos e não estou no lugar certo para usá-los.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
But there's nothing I can do to convince the naysayers, so I'm going to ask an adventurer <NAVI>[sir]<INFO>wolfvill,176,111,0,101,0</INFO></NAVI> to do it for me.|pt|Mas não há nada que eu possa fazer para convencer os pessimistas, então vou pedir a um aventureiro <NAVI>[sir]<INFO>wolfvill,176,111,0,101,0</INFO></NAVI> para fazer isso por mim.
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Please do, and in the meantime, I'll go meet some other people.|pt|Por favor, faça isso e, enquanto isso, irei conhecer outras pessoas.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
How about this? Don't push yourself for a while, eat good food, think good thoughts, and rest well, and you'll be able to walk or run lightly.|pt|Que tal isso? 
[Joel]|pt|[Joel]
Am I alive?? Am I alive?? Is my leg okay??|pt|Estou vivo?? 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Uh, since you say it is, it must be, right?|pt|Uh, já que você diz que é, deve ser, certo?
[Joel]|pt|[Joel]
Thank you so much!! You saved my boots! What's your name? I'll be good to you in the future. You're my savior. I never forget his saviors. For life.|pt|Muito obrigado!! 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
So, how did you save the leg?|pt|Então, como você salvou a perna?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Because that's what I learned. If the clinic had been properly equipped, we could have treated him more completely and accelerated his recovery.|pt|Porque foi isso que aprendi. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Hmm... Is that what everyone does these days?|pt|Hmm... É isso que todo mundo faz hoje em dia?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Yeah, it's not going to cost you your leg, as long as you treat it right.|pt|Sim, não vai custar sua perna, desde que você a trate bem.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
You can do that faster and more appropriately if you have a clinic, right?|pt|Você pode fazer isso de forma mais rápida e adequada se tiver uma clínica, certo?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Yes...? Isn't that right...?|pt|Sim...? 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Hmm... That's the way it is these days, isn't it, Adventurer?|pt|Hmm... É assim hoje em dia, não é, Aventureiro?
That's the way it is these days.|pt|É assim que acontece hoje em dia.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Like I said, it's not the technology of the foreigns, it's the technology and facilities of the advanced era.|pt|Como eu disse, não é a tecnologia dos estrangeiros, é a tecnologia e as instalações da era avançada.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Hmm, I don't think this is something you should just blindly oppose.|pt|Hmm, não acho que isso seja algo ao qual você deva se opor cegamente.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Right? That's my opinion too. It's about saving people. If we do it our way, we can save something from death.|pt|Certo? 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Hmm... How long would it take to build that clinic?|pt|Hmm... Quanto tempo levaria para construir aquela clínica?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Eh...? Well, it depends on labor and capital.|pt|Eh...? 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
We'll help you as much as we can. Let's build it.|pt|Nós o ajudaremos tanto quanto pudermos. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Instead, it should fit in with the way of life here, it should fit in with the place.|pt|Em vez disso, deveria se adequar ao modo de vida daqui, deveria se adequar ao lugar.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I see... I understand it.|pt|Entendo... eu entendo.
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Wow, you guys thought of everything. This is exactly what I need, and I'm all for it.|pt|Nossa, vocês pensaram em tudo. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Is there anything else we need here?|pt|Precisamos de mais alguma coisa aqui?
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
What, you're accepting more than clinics?|pt|O que, você está aceitando mais do que clínicas?
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Didn't that make you think? You have to go with the flow. You can't be stubborn forever.|pt|Isso não fez você pensar? 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
I mean, we're not going to live the way we do now, even if we do reclaim our land. We already live differently than we used to.|pt|Quero dizer, não vamos viver como vivemos agora, mesmo que recuperemos as nossas terras. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Hey, young man, if there's anything else that's important or necessary, let me know and we'll give it some thought.|pt|Ei, meu jovem, se houver mais alguma coisa importante ou necessária, me avise e pensaremos um pouco.
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
I will. I'll build the clinic as close to this place as possible, as you said.|pt|Eu vou. 
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Yeah. You know we're not going to live here forever, right?|pt|Sim. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Yes, that's exactly what I thought.|pt|Sim, foi exatamente isso que pensei.
[Old Man]|pt|[Old Man]
Well, we'll take our leave. Thank you for your time today.|pt|Bem, vamos nos despedir. 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Let's see!!!|pt|Vamos ver!!!
Whoa- that's a relief, isn't it?|pt|Uau, isso é um alívio, não é?
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Yeah, it's there... right? But it's so abrupt that it's a little baffling, isn't it?|pt|Sim, está aí... certo? 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
Now that they've seen it with their own eyes, they think differently. That's good. Now, let's finish what we started, shall we?|pt|Agora que viram com seus próprios olhos, eles pensam de forma diferente. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Yes. But first, I think we need to change the design to match this place. |pt|Sim. 
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
The Adventurer will help you, right?|pt|O Aventureiro vai te ajudar, certo?
That's... right...|pt|Isso mesmo...
[Maram]|pt|[Maram]
If you need any equipment or tools, let me know in advance and I'll bring them next time.|pt|Se precisar de algum equipamento ou ferramenta, avise-me com antecedência e trarei na próxima vez.
Joel, let's go get some rest, too.|pt|Joel, vamos descansar um pouco também.
[Joel]|pt|[Joel]
Goodbye, my savior. I'll be back in the near future!|pt|Adeus, meu salvador. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Adventurer, thank you so much for your help. This is what I got when I got settled here, and I don't need anything... I'll give it to you, Adventurer, as a token of my appreciation.|pt|Aventureiro, muito obrigado pela sua ajuda. 
[Ezekiel]|pt|[Ezekiel]
Well, until next time, and maybe I'll ask you for a favor, so stop by often!|pt|Bem, até a próxima, e talvez eu lhe peça um favor, então passe por aqui sempre!
